{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793299025,"nonce":"IDwvoTDQQPn6JiXm7h8jTVs5E5k=","title":"Keep preview cache stable when packaged tools are prepared","message":"Related: 4f691ccf9a2d1fcc01e7d19364ffa1c3240451d23e792ae41436a9871e4d9fc8\n\nThe real Worker -\u003e Rust runner -\u003e MSB -\u003e browser app preview run rendered Pocket Studio, but requesting an unchanged rebuild launched Haxe and Ash again. Linux packaged-tool preparation updates permissions, and preview input fingerprints included ctime/mtime as identity in addition to content. The toolchain also omitted TMPDIR, causing the CSS compiler to write .ashui/ashui-css into the Git workspace during compilation. Cache publication then sees changed inputs.\n\nUse metadata only to validate memoized content hashes; retain content, path, source/library inventory, compiler identity, runner flags and environment in build keys. Set the prepared Linux toolchain TMPDIR to /tmp. A regression must fail before the change when an unchanged bundled tool is prepared and rewritten, then preserve the key afterward. Actual source/library edits, changed tools/flags and corrupted cache outputs must still invalidate. Verify a real MSB browser rebuild reuses WASM without spawning a compiler.","files":null}]}